column1562:
08/Jul/26 4:41 AM;5f3432cde115420046434665;[~accountid:712020:f9a894b1-f824-4a33-a40d-1d507fe78d86] [~accountid:60ffd784627b560068a82355] [~accountid:712020:83d052d5-2c46-4e14-976e-37a61f730114] there is a lot happening here. I will do my best to describe what I am seeing…

# The rule on QA and the rule on PROD seem to be considerably different from one another. 
# Running the attached POA JSON against QA returns {{MC-00950963}} which is {{Mfg date: see on pack, with: A: day/month/year; B: month/year}}
# Running the attached POA JSON against PROD returns no elements.  
# When I examine the expected element to be returned and I compare it with the Rule on PROD…
## There are three instances of the expected output content ({{Mfg. date: See package.}}) within the input JSON.
### {{MC-00950964}}does not pass the test of Branch 1 because {{poa > rtaoriginmastercopy > classification}} is not empty.
### {{MC-00950964}} does not pass the test of Branch 2 because any of the value {{poa > productionPlant}} does not match any of the values of {{poa > rtaoriginmastercopy > plant}}
### {{MC-00950975}} does not pass the test of Branch 1 because {{poa > poaCategory}} does not match any of the values of {{poa > rtaoriginmastercopy > category}}
### {{MC-00950975}} does not pass the test of Branch 2 because {{poa > poaCategory}} does not match any of the values of {{poa > rtaoriginmastercopy > category}}
### {{MC-00950976}} does not pass the test of Branch 1 because {{poa > artWorkPlant}} is not empty.
### {{MC-00950976}} does not pass the test of Branch 2 because {{poa > poaShelfLifeMonths}} does not match any of the values of {{poa > rtaoriginmastercopy > mcShelfLifeMonths}}

Does my explanation of the behavior of this POA against the PROD Rule 1749 explain to your satisfaction why this element is not returned?  If not, what is the reason you feel it should have been returned?

column1565:
29/Jun/26 2:49 PM;5f3432cde115420046434665;[~accountid:712020:f9a894b1-f824-4a33-a40d-1d507fe78d86] 

{quote}If RM generates 1 MC with 4 LC, and in Copylist we have that MC already, with 5 LCs (4 of which match what we generated): we should we reuse that MC and 4 LCs that match.{quote}

So the 5th LC of the reused mastercopy is effectively discarded in the returned data. Correct?
